          "text": "# AG-UI Protocol Summary\n\n## Purpose\nAG-UI is \"an open, lightweight, event-based protocol that standardizes how AI agents connect to user-facing applications.\" It enables seamless integration between AI agents, real-time user context, and frontend interfaces.\n\n## Key Features\n- Real-time agentic chat with streaming\n- Bidirectional state synchronization\n- Generative UI and structured messaging\n- Real-time context enrichment\n- Frontend tool integration\n- Human-in-the-loop collaboration\n\n## Architecture & How It Works\n\n**Event-Based Design:**\nAgent backends emit events compatible with approximately 16 standard AG-UI event types. Agents can accept simple AG-UI-compatible inputs as arguments.\n\n**Middleware Layer:**\nThe protocol includes flexible middleware ensuring compatibility across diverse environments:\n- Works with any event transport (SSE, WebSockets, webhooks)\n- Enables loose event format matching for broad interoperability\n- Ships with reference HTTP implementation and default connector\n\n## Protocol Stack Position\nAG-UI complements other agentic protocols: MCP provides agents with tools, A2A enables agent-to-agent communication, while AG-UI brings agents into user-facing applications.\n\n## Implementation Support\nExtensive framework integrations include LangGraph, CrewAI, Google ADK, Microsoft Agent Framework, Pydantic AI, LlamaIndex, and others. SDKs available for Kotlin, Go, Dart, Java, and Rust. Licensed under MIT.",
