          "text": "# AG-UI Protocol Technical Details\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here's what's available about AG-UI's technical architecture:\n\n## Core Protocol Features\n\nAG-UI is described as an \"open, lightweight, event-based protocol\" designed for agent-human interaction. The specification indicates it standardizes \"how AI agents connect to user-facing applications.\"\n\n## Event System\n\nThe protocol operates through approximately 16 standard event types. Agents emit events compatible with these predefined categories, while backends accept \"one of a few simple AG-UI compatible inputs\" as arguments.\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe protocol supports:\n- Real-time streaming chat interactions\n- Bidirectional state synchronization between agents and interfaces\n- Generative UI with structured messaging\n- Live context enrichment\n- Frontend tool integration patterns\n- Human-in-the-loop collaboration features\n\n## Implementation Approach\n\nAG-UI includes a flexible middleware layer enabling compatibility across diverse transport mechanisms (SSE, WebSockets, webhooks) with \"loose event format matching\" to support broad interoperability.\n\n## Documentation Limitation\n\nThe webpage primarily references external resources rather than detailing technical specifications. For comprehensive information about specific message formats, TypeScript implementations, or state synchronization mechanisms, the documentation directs readers to [docs.ag-ui.com](https://docs.ag-ui.com) and the [AG-UI Dojo](https://dojo.ag-ui.com/) demonstration environment.",
