          "text": "# AG-UI Core SDK Technical Overview\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here's what's available in the `@ag-ui/core` package:\n\n## Core Components\n\nThe SDK operates on a **\"streaming event-based architecture with strongly typed data structures.\"** This foundation enables real-time communication between agent systems and user interfaces.\n\n## Type System\n\nThe package defines five primary data structures:\n\n1. **RunAgentInput** - Configuration and parameters for agent execution\n2. **Message** - Handles bidirectional communication and tool invocations\n3. **Context** - Information provided to agents during operation\n4. **Tool** - Specifications for callable functions agents can access\n5. **State** - Agent state tracking and management\n\n## Event Categories\n\nThe protocol organizes events into five classifications:\n\n- **Lifecycle Events** - Monitor run and step progression\n- **Text Message Events** - Stream assistant responses incrementally\n- **Tool Call Events** - Track function invocation stages\n- **State Management Events** - Propagate agent state changes\n- **Special Events** - Raw and custom event handling\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @ag-ui/core\n```\n\n## Note on Documentation\n\nThe provided content references complete type and event documentation but doesn't include actual interface definitions, protocol specifications, usage examples, or implementation details about agent event emission, tool registration mechanisms, or state synchronization workflows. Those technical specifics would be found in the linked reference pages.",
