          "text": "# TypeScript Type Definitions Summary\n\n## RunAgentInput\n\"Input parameters for running an agent. In the HTTP API, this is the body of the `POST` request.\"\n\nProperties:\n- `threadId` (string): ID of the conversation thread\n- `runId` (string): ID of the current run\n- `parentRunId?` (string): ID of the run that spawned this run\n- `state` (any): Current state of the agent\n- `messages` (Message[]): Array of messages in the conversation\n- `tools` (Tool[]): Array of tools available to the agent\n- `context` (Context[]): Array of context objects provided to the agent\n- `forwardedProps` (any): \"Additional properties forwarded to the agent\"\n\n## Message\nA union type encompassing six distinct message varieties: DeveloperMessage, SystemMessage, AssistantMessage, UserMessage, ToolMessage, and ActivityMessage. Each includes an `id` (string) and `role` field with role-specific values.\n\n## Context\nTwo-property structure for contextual information:\n- `description` (string): \"Description of what this context represents\"\n- `value` (string): The actual context value\n\n## Tool\nDefines agent-callable functionality with three properties:\n- `name` (string): Name of the tool\n- `description` (string): \"Description of what the tool does\"\n- `parameters` (any): \"JSON Schema defining the parameters for the tool\"\n\n## State\n\"The state type is flexible and can hold any data structure needed by the agent implementation.\" Defined as `any`.",
